# Ranges that are ALLOWED to have stopped being built from source.
#
# tools/source_coverage.py --check fails when the bytes this repo compiles out of src/
# go DOWN, because a range that stops being `complete` in a delinks.txt is refilled by
# dsd with retail cartridge bytes and the ROM still matches perfectly -- no other gate
# in the tree can see it.
#
# A decrease is sometimes CORRECT, though: a fakematch retracted, a file demoted to a
# ROM-byte placeholder because its match turned out to be a relocation artefact, an
# entry removed because the range belonged to another module. Those are the tree
# getting more honest. Record them here rather than leaving a known-bad match enrolled
# to keep a number up.
#
# One JSON object per line. Every field is required; a row with no `reason` is rejected
# loudly, not honoured -- an unexplained waiver is exactly the failure this gate exists
# to prevent.
#
#   {"module": "ov010", "section": ".text", "start": "0x021e4f00",
#    "end": "0x021e4f80", "reason": "func_021e4f00 was a fakematch; demoted in #1234"}
#
# Waivers are consumed ONCE. After the decrease lands, main's own total is the new floor
# and the row does nothing; stale rows are harmless and can be pruned in a later sweep.
#
{"module": "arm9", "section": ".rodata", "start": "0x02075f14", "end": "0x02082158", "reason": "particle resource is supplied from the cartridge image; source only takes its address"}
{"module": "arm9", "section": ".data", "start": "0x0208a178", "end": "0x0208c178", "reason": "font is supplied from the cartridge image; source only takes its address"}
{"module": "arm9", "section": ".data", "start": "0x0209289c", "end": "0x0209435c", "reason": "message tables are supplied from the cartridge image; Message3 only takes their addresses"}

{"module": "ov021", "section": ".rodata", "start": "0x02114740", "end": "0x02114748", "reason": "section-kind correction: sNewsLiftPlatformYaws is mutable .data in retail (sits in the .data run immediately before the news-lift RTTI); the const spelling was the bug. The same bytes remain source-built, now honestly as .data"}
{"module": "ov047", "section": ".rodata", "start": "0x02111ab4", "end": "0x02111ad4", "reason": "section-kind correction: gKm3KurumaClps sits physically inside the contiguous stage-map .data in retail; its bytes remain source-built as .data by the same d_s_map_ov047.c claim, so the .rodata family decrease is a reclassification, not a coverage loss"}
{"module": "ov047", "section": ".rodata", "start": "0x02111b54", "end": "0x02111b74", "reason": "section-kind correction: gKm3KurumajikuClps sits physically inside the contiguous stage-map .data in retail; its bytes remain source-built as .data by the same d_s_map_ov047.c claim, so the .rodata family decrease is a reclassification, not a coverage loss"}
